---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Import collections (Postman, Insomnia, Bruno, HAR, .http, OpenAPI) and curl commands

Usage: rustman import [OPTIONS] [SRC]
       rustman import <COMMAND>

Commands:
  curl         Convert a curl command (an argument, or stdin) into a request file
  auto         Import a source file or folder, detecting its format from the content
  postman      Import a Postman Collection v2.0 or v2.1 export
  postman-env  Import a Postman environment export into environments/
  insomnia     Import an Insomnia v4 (JSON) or v5 (YAML) export
  bruno        Import a Bruno collection folder (or a single .bru file)
  har          Import the requests of a HAR 1.2 capture, grouped by host
  http         Import .http / .rest files (a file or a folder) and their environments
  openapi      Create a collection from an OpenAPI 3.0 or 3.1 document (a file or URL)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [SRC]
          A source file or folder whose format is detected from its content

Options:
      --into <DIR>
          Collection folder to write into, inside the workspace (default: the slug of the source collection's name)

      --dry-run
          Convert and print the planned files and secrets without writing anything

      --on-conflict <POLICY>
          When a file already exists: keep it, replace it, or write next to it
          
          [default: skip]
          [possible values: skip, overwrite, rename]

      --report <FILE>
          Also write the report as JSON (rustman.import-report/v1) to FILE

      --migration-report <FILE>
          Write the unconverted script statements, with suggestions, as Markdown to FILE

      --max-size <SIZE>
          Refuse sources larger than this (bytes, or with K, M or G; default 100M)

      --fail-on-unsupported
          Exit with 1 when a feature was unsupported, dropped or unmapped

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
